\begin{abstract}
We present APOLLO-CM, a centimeter-resolution astrometric and cosmological
simulation engine that integrates relativistic gravitational dynamics,
quantum-CM field coupling, magnetohydrodynamics (MHD), and exascale
orchestration into a unified high-fidelity cosmological manifold. The system
ingests heterogeneous astrophysical datasets (CNG, JWST, DESI, cosmological
logs) through a Centimeter Ontology (CMO) parser, constructs a centimeter-scale
vector lattice, and evolves coupled gravitational, quantum, and fluid fields
under strict energy and Hamiltonian conservation constraints. Verification
metrics demonstrate Hamiltonian drift $\Delta H/H_0 < 10^{-18}$, energy
conservation $\Delta E/E < 10^{-10}$, quantum fidelity $F > 1 - 10^{-9}$, and
ontological compliance at 99.99\%. APOLLO-CM thus functions as a candidate
centimeter-resolved cosmological law engine.
\end{abstract}

