\section{Relativistic Gravitational Dynamics}

The relativistic kernel evolves the centimeter-resolved manifold using
modified Friedmann and field equations. N-body motion is governed by:
\begin{equation}
\frac{\partial^2 \mathbf{r}}{\partial t^2} = S_a(\mathbf{r}),
\qquad
\frac{\partial \mathbf{v}}{\partial t} = S_r(\mathbf{v}),
\end{equation}
where $S_a$ and $S_r$ encode gravitational and relativistic source terms.

Tensor evolution is expressed as:
\begin{equation}
G_{\mu\nu}(\text{cm}) =
\frac{\partial}{\partial t}
\left(
\frac{\partial T_{\mu\nu}}{\partial t}
\right),
\end{equation}
with subgrid energy terms:
\begin{equation}
E_{\text{MHD}}(\text{cm}) =
\frac{\partial}{\partial t}
\left(
\frac{\partial T}{\partial t}
\right),
\end{equation}
coupling metric evolution to fluid and magnetic energy densities.

